seg-c1a27b995345 = Kshana implements the spreading codes and the message layer of the LunaNet <b>Augmented Forward Signal (AFS)</b> as one edition of the specification defines them, and checks itself against that edition's printed tables.

# text
# c1: 986e0795…e61b6
seg-e9bd99bbddb5 = <b>Pin.</b> LunaNet Interoperability Specification (LNIS) <b>Version { "5" }</b>, Applicable Document { "1" } Volume A: <em>LunaNet Signal-In-Space Recommended Standard, Augmented Forward Signal</em> (LSIS-AFS) <b>Version { "1.0" }, { "29" } January { "2025" }</b> (NASA). Retrieved 2026-10-18; PDF SHA-256 <c1/> (<a1>provenance</a1>). A later edition is a different pin and may change the codes: the document marks its code tables { "{" }LSIS-TBC{ "}" } and says they are "included to facilitate test and integration efforts only". Every report names this edition.

